{offset0}Deciphering: {arialbld}Chief Barkod{arial}

from: Markus Boggus

to: {rank} {name}









Local resistance leaders Wilfrid Bang and Rolf Olfulsen have informed us of an upcoming heavy water delivery. These courageous men once succeeded at sabotaging the factory. The Tektons worked day and night over six months to repair the damage.{pause}

Are the Psychos ever paying the price for producing this accursed water! It's needed for special bombs. It's said that a single of these bombs could entirely annihilate a city. A bomb filled with water! It's insane!{pause}

But if it is possible, I can't believe that men could be sick enough to drop such a bomb on a city!{pause} On civilians, on women, on children.{pause} If this were to happen, it would be an abominable crime... against humanity itself.{pause} 


This must not happen. My men and I are ready to do whatever it takes to prevent this.{pause}

Will you come with us, {rank} {name}, {arialbld}to stop this from happening?{arial}{pause}


{offset150}Commander of the Mutinous Vessel Graff-Spitz.



{offset200}{signature6}{offset0}{pause}{pause}


(1)Hydrogen Bomb:{micro}

Professor Robert Onestone has proved the existence of colossal forces inside the atoms which make up matter.{pause}

Theoretically, if two atoms (nucleons) collide extremely violently and their nuclei manage to "touch", they fuse together - "nuclear fusion".{pause}

Normally this never happens, since the nuclei of these atoms, being positive, repel and forces binding the protons to the neutrons are stronger than anything.{pause}

This process nevertheless happens perpetually in our sun, which essentially consists of hydrogen gas. The pressure at the surface of the sun is so tremendous that the highly compressed hydrogen atoms fuse.{pause}

When the phenomenal force separating the two hydrogen nuclei is overcome, THEN, suddenly, they are attracted, and WHOOSH! They fuse together in a flash of energy, becoming a single helium atom.{pause}

The energy released at this instant is even stronger than that required for the atoms to touch. So much so that if there are other hydrogen atoms nearby, they fuse as well, and so on, until there's no more hydrogen. Just like a candle will burn as long as there's wax.{pause}

Except that the flame of this candle is so powerful that Onestone's calculations are difficult for a human mind to truly appreciate.{pause}

The difficulty however lies with the "detonator" to light the candle, as hydrogen must be raised to a temperature of many million degrees to activate fusion!{pause}

A hydrogen isotope such as deuterium would make an ideal fuel for such a bomb. Deuterium is found in "heavy water", that's the story!{pause}


By Chief Barkod,
at your service {rank} {name}.
